#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 08 Verify: an outsider reproduces every finding of the run, offline, from the run's bundle alone.

Usage: 08-verify --population DIR --out RUN/08-verify

RUN is the loop run (the parent of --out). For each other `<NN>-<name>/` in it
this step, with no account and no network call:

  integrity     the finding passes steps/finding.py's check (every proof file it
                names is there and matches its sha256), it is of this run's
                population, and every key its proof relies on is the key the
                repository lists for that party (population/<p>/, never a key
                read from the bundle);
  reproduction  the files the finding names in `proof`, and only those, are
                copied into a scratch `<NN>-<name>/`, and the step's own judge,
                loaded read-only from steps/, decides again on them: the
                re-derived result and not_checked list must be the recorded
                ones. The judges re-run the signature, checkpoint and inclusion
                checks with the step's pinned verifiers (all local), so those
                are re-run on the cited bytes under the repository's keys. A
                mismatch is a FAIL naming the step.
  coverage      a step whose proof is not enough to re-derive its result (its
                judge needs bytes the finding does not cite, a live data dir, or
                a verifier not installed here) is never passed on trust: it is a
                not_checked entry {what, why, issue} saying what is missing.
  live          live steps 01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 07 and 09 are re-derived the
                same way: their judges read only their proof (and, for 07, the
                repository's nodes/ listings; listed keys and 03's carrier
                bytes are held to this checkout). The other live steps' judges
                read a lab node's data dir or console, so they are not_checked
                (evidence-network/loop#188).

The finding is FAIL when any step fails integrity or reproduction, NOT_CHECKED
when every step present held but one or more could not be reproduced, and PASS
only when every step present was integrity-checked and reproduced.
verified.json, beside the finding, is the manifest steps 10 and 11 read: per
step, its recorded and re-derived result and not_checked, its status, what did
not hold, and the sha256 of every file this step read (finding.json and each
proof file).

What each step's proof is, and how its judge is re-run, is steps/08-verify.md.
Exit 0 once the finding is written, whatever the result.
"""
